{"nodes": [{"id": "agents_plans_prd_005_rbac_completed_story_016_startup_bootstrap_guard_plan_doc", "label": "Plan: Fail-fast startup guard when RBAC is enabled with no seeded users", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".agents/plans/PRD-005-rbac/completed/STORY-016-startup-bootstrap-guard.plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_fail_fast_bootstrap_guard", "label": "Fail-fast RBAC bootstrap guard (check_bootstrap)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/plans/PRD-005-rbac/completed/STORY-016-startup-bootstrap-guard.plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "check_bootstrap() raises RbacNotBootstrappedError when RBAC_ENABLED=true and count_active_users()==0, naming the exact scripts/manage_users.py create-user command to fix it. It deliberately does not treat a configured ADMIN_TOKEN as sufficient bootstrap, since identity.resolve() can synthesize an admin identity from ADMIN_TOKEN without any row in the users table -- so a deployment could otherwise appear to boot successfully while being usable only via one break-glass credential and unusable for anyone else."}], "edges": [{"source": "agents_plans_prd_005_rbac_completed_story_016_startup_bootstrap_guard_plan_doc", "target": "app_services_authz", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/plans/PRD-005-rbac/completed/STORY-016-startup-bootstrap-guard.plan.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_plans_prd_005_rbac_completed_story_016_startup_bootstrap_guard_plan_doc", "target": "app_main", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/plans/PRD-005-rbac/completed/STORY-016-startup-bootstrap-guard.plan.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_plans_prd_005_rbac_complete